 "decoder_spec": "Lookup-table (coset-leader) decoder. FULL (untruncated) FIFO BFS over the syndrome space {0,1}^n_det from syndrome 0 (weight 0, predicted observable 0), mechanisms applied in canonical index order; first assignment wins. Decoder output D(s) = pred[s]. A fault set F is correctable iff D(sigma(F)) == obs(F). The detector masks span the syndrome space, so every syndrome is assigned. Identical on weight-<=WMAX syndromes to the depth-truncated BFS of the Part H certificates.",
 "masks_span_syndrome_space": true,
 "method": "Syndrome-space character sums (Walsh-Hadamard transforms). For y in F_2^{n+1}, a(y) = #{j : <y,v_j> = 0} with v_j = (d_j, o_j). Counting: A_w = 2^{-(n+1)} sum_y I^(y) g_w(a(y)), g_w(k) = [t^w](1+t)^k(1-t)^{m-k}. Probability: P_L = 2^{-(n+1)} sum_y I^(y) prod_{j:<y,v_j>=1}(1-2 p_j), exact in integer arithmetic over the dyadic common denominator. I^ is the transform of the failure indicator [b != D(s)]. The checker re-derives both from the mechanism list alone.",
